# Flex Component Responsive Props

Yes, the Flex component fully supports responsive object values. According to the documentation:

> "Flex component props can have responsive values the same way as other style props"

**Example:**

```tsx
import { Flex, Button } from '@mantine/core';

function Demo() {
  return (
    <Flex
      direction={{ base: 'column', sm: 'row' }}
      gap={{ base: 'sm', sm: 'lg' }}
      justify={{ sm: 'center' }}
    >
      <Button>Button 1</Button>
      <Button>Button 2</Button>
      <Button>Button 3</Button>
    </Flex>
  );
}
```

This demonstrates that `direction`, `gap`, `justify`, and other flexbox properties can use breakpoint-based objects to change layout behavior across different screen sizes. This is one key advantage distinguishing Flex from the simpler Group and Stack components.

